    "exit_rule": "red on the pad and drawer_position > 0.26 at the final state",
    "guidance": "Low-confidence red-centered specialist, not a routine default. In the fixed in-distribution protocol it passed 4/12 runs. Invoke only from its supported state: drawer_position strictly >0.26 m, red exposed, and a reliable current red pose, with entry at the drawer front or during red approach/contact/lift. Its red-frame representation is intended for red-pose displacement, but no displaced-red validation exists. Avoid after red release, when blue/post-release geometry dominates, when the red pose is stale, or when transformed targets may be obstructed/unreachable. Treat lack of red/TCP co-motion after closing, IK non-convergence, low carried-red motion into furniture, red outside the pad or following retreat, or drawer_position falling to <=0.26 as failure. Validation failures ended either with red off-pad (5 runs) or red on-pad but the drawer below threshold (3 runs); several had hundreds of unconverged IK steps. Three failed runs transiently met the exit rule and later lost it, so verify the fixed condition at handoff rather than accepting a transient pass. Handoff: require red contained on the pad and no longer following TCP while drawer_position remains >0.26; the retained overlap can continue into blue pickup, with observed blue/TCP co-motion on initial lift as the cleanest cue to switch to blue_insert."
  },
